# TraceDecay operational boundaries

Use TraceDecay when its graph, durable memory, or session evidence answers the
task. Known-file reads, ordinary local edits, nonindexed material, and questions
requiring clarification can use the appropriate native workflow directly.

Read freshness and coverage with results; an empty index result does not prove
absence. Preserve exact project/worktree selectors and opaque continuation or
mutation identities. Cross-project operations must use the selected registered
store, not whichever project is active.

MCP and CLI share daemon authority. A transport failure may use the equivalent
CLI operation when the daemon remains available. Preserve an unavailable or
intentionally held daemon and report the limitation. Private database reads are
not a supported fallback.

Preview and read results do not grant mutation authority. Apply, cancellation,
and rollback consume their returned identities and typed state; reconcile
committed effects before retrying an interrupted operation.
